# Ruby
example/vendor/

# Ignored to stop `git add -A` from recommitting the one this machine can
# produce, not because a lockfile is unwanted. macOS ships Ruby 2.6.10, whose
# Bundler writes `BUNDLED WITH 1.17.2`; a current Bundler honours that line by
# re-execing 1.17.2, which dies calling String#untaint (removed in Ruby 3.2).
# That turned build-ios red for the whole of 0.1.0's release run. Delete these
# two lines and commit the file once one can be generated on a current Ruby —
# `turbo.json` already hashes it when present.
example/Gemfile.lock

